sentences.l:
and Phylo brought a silver basket, which for her had set
Alcandre, Polybus’ wife, who dwelt in Thebes,
Egyptian, where most of all, in houses, treasures lie stored;

Argive Helen wept, sprung of Zeus,
and Telemachus wept, and Atreus' son Menelaus,
nor indeed did Nestor's son keep his two eyes tearless;

for I, at least,
take no delight in mourning after supper, but also, dawn
will be early-born;

for of such a father too you are, seeing that prudent things you speak as well,
and easily known is the offspring of a man for whom Cronus' son
spins good fortune, both at his marrying and at his begetting,
